      "value": "Requirements extracted from Zimmermann Functional Requirements excel, downloaded July 3rd, 2026 after all requirements were confirmed. — source of truth. Req ID prefix: **REG**.\n\n⚠️ **Rows with strikethrough are out of scope** — struck through in the Excel source file.\n\n|  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Req ID | Functional Area | Sub-Functional Area | Requirement | Owner | Storefront | Config/Custom | Status | Comments |\n| REG-001 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Storefront Configuration | The system will support 7 independent storefronts in SFCC Business Manager (AU, US (Domestic & International), UK, EU Domestic, EU International, HK, ME), each configured as a separate site. | Accenture | ALL | Config | Confirmed | Confirmed 8 storefronts |\n| REG-002 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Storefront Configuration | The system will assign each storefront its own currency, tax display model, locale set, delivery options, and payment methods, configured independently in SFCC Business Manager. | Accenture | ALL | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| REG-003 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Storefront Configuration | The AU storefront will operate on a domestic checkout path (SFCC-owned), serving Australia and NZ/Oceania customers in AUD. | Accenture | AU | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| REG-004 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Storefront Configuration | The UK storefront will operate on a domestic checkout path (SFCC-owned), serving the United Kingdom in GBP. | Accenture | UK | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| REG-005 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Storefront Configuration | The US storefront will support both a domestic checkout path (SFCC-owned) and an international checkout path (Global-e-owned) within the same site; the path is determined by the customer's shipping address | Accenture | US | Custom | Confirmed | 8 storefronts (US International and Domestic separate) |\n| REG-006 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Storefront Configuration | The system will process all orders placed on the EU domestic storefront through the SFCC domestic checkout path, serving EU customers in EUR | Accenture | EU dom | Config | Confirmed | The EU Dom site needs to be able to support one RRP, however multiple EU zone VAT requirements in order payload. To confirm if Avalara is going to handle this? |\n| REG-006 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Storefront Configuration | The system will process all orders placed on the EU international storefront through a Global-e owned checkout path, with currency determined by the customer's shipping address. The EU domestic and EU international storefronts are separate storefronts | Accenture | EU Int | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| REG-007 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Storefront Configuration | The HK storefront will operate as a Global-e-only checkout storefront; all checkout, payment, and tax handling is managed by Global-e. | Accenture | HK | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| REG-008 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Storefront Configuration | The ME storefront will operate as a Global-e-only checkout storefront; all checkout, payment, and tax handling is managed by Global-e. | Accenture | ME | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| REG-009 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Storefront Configuration | The AU storefront is gated; it is accessible to AU and NZ/Pacific Island IP addresses only. | Accenture | AU | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| REG-010 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Storefront Configuration | The system will allow business users to manage storefront configuration in SFCC Business Manager at both a global level (applying across all storefronts) and at an individual storefront level. | Accenture | ALL | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| REG-011 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Storefront Configuration | The system will display locale-specific additional fields at the billing address step where required by market (e.g. Italian fiscal code (Codice Fiscale) or VAT ID for the Italian locale). | Accenture | EU | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| REG-012 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Storefront Configuration | The system will support all required US address formats on the US storefront. The system will not support APO, FPO or PO Box addresses | Accenture | US | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| REG-013 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Storefront Configuration | The system will automatically route customers to the correct regional storefront based on IP geolocation on site entry | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| REG-014 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Country Slide Out | The system will detect a mismatch between the customer's IP-detected country and the current storefront's shipping region on site entry. | Accenture | ALL (excl. AU) | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| REG-015 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Country Slide Out | The system will display a country slide-out when a shipping location mismatch is detected, informing the customer that they appear to be visiting from a different location. This will show only if the customer is accessing a different storefront. The customer can dismiss the selector and continue browsing on their current storefront without making a change | Accenture | ALL (excl. AU) | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| REG-016 | Regional Storefronts, Multi-Language, GDPR & Consent | Country Slide Out | The system will present two CTAs within the slide-out: one to redirect the customer to the appropriate storefront for their detected location, and one to open the country selector to manually change their shipping country. | Accenture | ALL (excl. AU) |